# Fantasy Friends — line-ending contract.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS
#   The migration guard pins a SHA-256 for every reviewed design draft. On Linux
#   and macOS those files are checked out with LF; on Windows, `core.autocrlf=true`
#   (the Git for Windows default) rewrites them to CRLF in the working tree while
#   the blob stays LF. `git status` therefore reports a clean tree, but any tool
#   that reads the file from disk sees different bytes. That mismatch produced 24
#   spurious guard failures on Windows against a green CI.
#
#   The guard now normalises line endings before hashing, so it is correct either
#   way. This file additionally makes the checkout deterministic, so what is on
#   disk matches what a reviewer sees in the diff.
#
# SQL and generated artefacts are pinned to LF deliberately: these files are
# hashed, re-derived from source, and applied verbatim by the Supabase CLI.
# Changing this can silently invalidate every pinned hash on the project.

* text=auto eol=lf

*.sql   text eol=lf
*.mjs   text eol=lf
*.ts    text eol=lf
*.tsx   text eol=lf
*.json  text eol=lf
*.md    text eol=lf
*.toml  text eol=lf
*.css   text eol=lf
*.yml   text eol=lf
*.example text eol=lf

# Binary files must never be line-ending converted.
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.webp  binary
*.ico   binary
*.dump  binary
